=2 Walkthrough
!Caedarva Mire-map2.jpg|right|Caedarva Mire (Map 2)
!Arrapago Reef-map5.jpg|right|Arrapago Reef (Map 5)
\**{c=red:Note:}** All members of your party (including any who have finished this mission before) need an {k:Ephramadian gold coin} to enter the battlefield during this mission. If you need another gold coin, examine **Jazaraat's Headstone** at {z:Caedarva Mire} (E-10).
* Head to the Cutter, which is located at (H-8) on {p:Map 5|https://www.bg-wiki.com/ffxi/File:Arrapago_Reef-map5.jpg} of {z:Arrapago Reef}. There are a few options for getting there:
** The {i:Arrapago Ring|Arrapago Ring|26235}, purchased with 100 {p:Imperial standing accolades}, will teleport you in front of the Cutter. It will only work if you've been to the zone before but is the fastest route if true.
** Take the {p:Survival Guide} to {z:Caedarva Mire} and run south to zone into {z:Arrapago Reef} at (G-8).
*** Note this is NOT the (G-6) zone to {z:Arrapago Reef} just east of where you teleport in from the {p:Survival Guide}
*** After zoning, head south to (H-8 on Map 5) to find the Cutter.
** Grab an {i:Imperial Silver Piece|Imperial Silver Piece|2185} (or just 200 Standing), take the Runic Portal to {z:Dvucca Isle Staging Point} to {z:Caedarva Mire} (Map 2) and head West to the (F-9) entrance to {z:Arrapago Reef}. You'll have to pay the entrance fee. Once inside, head North to (H-8) to find the Cutter.

* Approach the Cutter for a cutscene.
* When you are ready, Examine the Cutter to enter a battlefield.
* After the fight, you will wind up in {z:Nashmau}.
** Players who have already completed this mission will end up back at the Cutter instead.

=2 Battlefield
* {p:Gessho} will assist you in this fight. Trusts may also be summoned.
** {p:Gessho} will wait a minute or two before he begins to fight. This gives your party a little time to buff.
** The fight will continue even if {p:Gessho} is killed.
* The first phase of battle is against the {m:Ashu Talif Crew}, which consists of 2x {p:Rangers|Ranger}, 2x {p:Red Mages|Red Mage}, and 1x {p:Corsair}.
** The {m:Ashu Talif Crew} seem to be resistant to most forms of sleep unless {p:Elemental Seal} is used first.
** {p:Lullaby} was easily landed in {p:Item Level} 119 equipment.
* Once the five {m:Ashu Talif Crew} members are defeated, another four will take their place.
* The {m:Ashu Talif Captain} will spawn along with the others after a moment.
* You must bring the {m:Ashu Talif Captain}'s health to approximately 20% to win the battle.

